# SNS Studio Integration 4017 runtime identity (SSOT)
#
# Copy these three keys into the dedicated runtime's .env.integration
# (the directory passed as -IntegrationRuntimeDirectory). They are the single
# source of truth for:
#   - docker-compose.sns-studio-integration-media.yaml  (${...} interpolation)
#   - scripts/windows/start-sns-studio.ps1               (resolved-config and
#                                                         running-container checks)
#
# Rules
#   - No fallback: if a key is missing, Compose and the launcher fail closed.
#   - The uploads volume must already exist. The launcher never creates it and
#     never falls back to another (legacy) volume name.
#   - Images must already exist locally. The launcher never pulls/builds or
#     falls back to an older known tag.
#
# Updating after an Integration HEAD change that needs a new image
#   1. Build and tag the new images from the target Integration commit, e.g.
#        sns-studio/integration-4017:unified-<shortsha>
#   2. Update SNS_STUDIO_INTEGRATION_IMAGE / SNS_STUDIO_MEDIA_WORKER_IMAGE
#      below (in .env.integration) to the new tags.
#   3. Recreate only the affected containers in a controlled maintenance step
#      (the launcher only starts existing containers; it reports a running
#      container whose image differs from the SSOT as STALE and stops).
#   4. Run the launcher; it re-verifies identity and refreshes its safe marker.
#
# Placeholders below are intentionally not real values: the actual identity
# literals live only in the runtime's .env.integration.
SNS_STUDIO_INTEGRATION_IMAGE=sns-studio/integration-4017:<verified-tag>
SNS_STUDIO_MEDIA_WORKER_IMAGE=sns-studio/media-worker:<verified-tag>
SNS_STUDIO_UPLOADS_VOLUME=<existing-canonical-uploads-volume>
